cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "MicroCLR: Contrastive Learning for Microbiome-Based Disease Classification"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20751445"  # update to the new version DOI after Zenodo release
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hguzzi/MicroCLR"
url: "https://github.com/hguzzi/MicroCLR"

abstract: >
  MicroCLR is a SimCLR-based contrastive self-supervised learning framework for
  gut microbiome disease classification. It implements eight biologically-motivated
  and generic data augmentation strategies for CLR-transformed metagenomic profiles,
  and benchmarks learned representations on four diseases (colorectal cancer, type 2
  diabetes, inflammatory bowel disease, Parkinson's disease) across seven cohorts
  under within-cohort cross-validation, leave-one-cohort-out generalization, and
  low-label fine-tuning protocols. Two novel augmentations are introduced:
  EcologicalAug (Spearman co-occurrence network-guided community perturbation) and
  CohortStyleAug (inter-cohort mean-shift style transfer).

